The automatic sequence: down, grip, up, right, down, release, up, left — starting from top-left position. So states 0..7 or 1..8:
1. Down (until DownLimitSwitch)
2. Grip (until GripLimitSwitch)
3. Up (until UpLimitSwitch)
4. Right (until RightLimitSwitch)
5. Down (until DownLimitSwitch)
6. Release (until ReleaseLimitSwitch)
7. Up (until UpLimitSwitch)
8. Left (until LeftLimitSwitch) — then back to start (top-left).

Manual mode: each button commands its matching action only while the corresponding limit switch is not active. So MoveDown := DownButton AND NOT DownLimitSwitch; etc. Grip command while NOT GripLimitSwitch, Release while NOT ReleaseLimitSwitch. Also never command opposing directions at the same time — in manual mode with buttons, Up and Down could both be pressed; we need to prevent opposing commands simultaneously. We can prioritize: MoveUp := UpButton AND NOT DownButton... Actually "Never command opposing directions at the same time" — we should ensure MoveDown AND MoveUp not both TRUE. Simple approach: prioritize Up over Down and Left over Right (or make each pair exclusive). Let's implement: downCmd := DownButton AND NOT UpButton AND NOT DownLimitSwitch; upCmd := UpButton AND NOT DownButton AND NOT UpLimitSwitch; similarly left/right.

Emergency stop active-low: when EmergencyStop = FALSE, immediately set all six action outputs FALSE and do not advance the automatic sequence. We should also clear the run flags/step state? "do not advance the automatic sequence" — hold the sequence at current step; the outputs go off. When E-stop released (TRUE again), presumably the sequence pauses at same step and can resume on Start? The review notes say behavior must be frozen. I'll implement: on E-stop, outputs off, sequence paused (state retained), run flags cleared so a new Start edge is needed to resume in single-step/single-cycle; in continuous mode maybe require new Start too. Simpler: keep state, clear running flag; when Start rising edge while E-stop ok, set running flag (and for single-cycle reset step to 0? Hmm).

